module nova_native_driver_entry;
import nova_native_driver;

// THE APPLICATION ENTRY OF THE NATIVE DRIVER, and why it declares no function.
//
// This is the tests/ entry that names the driver's application module. The
// MODULE-SET census of tests_ntasm_abi.c reads exactly that: a module joins the
// set by being given an entry under tests/nova/tests that names it,
// and a module of the directory with no such entry is reported by name. The
// name below is also resolved against the compiler's own inputs, so a module
// absent from the compile is refused with "Nova imported module is not among
// compiler inputs" at nova.c's module_headers, instead of being a string a
// harness wrote down and nobody checks against the tree.
//
// It declares no `main` and no other function ON PURPOSE. The driver's own
// `export fn main()->u64` IS the application: public_entry_v2 (nova.c,
// "Nova ABI2 main is ambiguous across modules") refuses a program carrying two,
// and the seed harness runs the driver's, with zero parameters, as the ABI2
// wrapper's `$nova_body`. A helper here would add a symbol and a function slot
// to the seed image that no contract owns, so this entry contributes the edge
// and nothing else -- which is also why adding it cannot move a byte of the
// driver's OUTPUT.EFI.
